# The how-to guide

`docs/HOW-TO.md` is the complete operator's manual: every screen, every control,
every workflow, illustrated. A change to the interface that leaves the guide
behind is an unfinished change.

Write it under `documentation-style`: present tense, assertive, no changelog
framing. Replace the paragraph that described the old behaviour instead of
adding a note beside it.

## When the interface changes

1. Edit the section of `docs/HOW-TO.md` that covers the screen. Keep it
   task-shaped — a heading a user would search for, then the steps.
2. Re-photograph the app:

   ```bash
   npm run docs:screenshots
   ```

3. Prove the guide still covers everything:

   ```bash
   npm run docs:check
   ```

Both commands are also run by `.github/workflows/docs.yml`, so skipping them
fails the build rather than shipping a stale guide.

## How the screenshots work

`scripts/docs/capture.mjs` serves the real app with Vite, answers the Rust side
from the demo book in `scripts/docs/fixtures.mjs`, freezes the clock at
`TODAY`, walks each route, opens each dialog, and sizes the window to the
content. Every picture in the guide comes from that run — none is taken by hand.

- **A new screen or dialog**: add a shot to the `shots` array in
  `capture.mjs` with its caption, and reference `screenshots/<name>.png` from
  the guide. The check fails on a shot that no one shows and on an image the
  capture script does not produce.
- **A new command**: answer it in `scripts/docs/mock-tauri.mjs`. An unanswered
  command throws, and the shot lands on an error state.
- **New data on screen**: extend `fixtures.mjs` rather than special-casing the
  page. Dashboard totals, tab counts and list contents are all derived from
  that one dataset, so they agree with each other.
- Keep the demo book fictional. No real client names, numbers or policy
  numbers ever go into a screenshot.

## What `docs:check` enforces

- Every route in `src/App.tsx` is named in the guide.
- Every sidebar item in `src/components/AppShell.tsx` is named in the guide.
- Every `<Button>` label in `src/pages/**` is explained, except the generic ones
  listed in `scripts/docs/check-guide.mjs`.
- The screenshots on disk, the screenshots in the guide, and the shots the
  capture script takes are the same set.

Add a label to the generic list only when it genuinely carries no meaning of its
own. Documenting the operation is the cheaper fix.
